{"seconds": 70.4, "exit": 0, "final": "After Kh1, Black has fxe1=Q+ which is check. That wins material immediately. So exf2+ is definitely the move.\n\nThe best line is:\n1...exf2+ 2.Kg2 f1=Q+ (or 2.Kh1 fxe1=Q+ or other alternatives leading to similar wins)\n\n**Coaching explanation:**\nThe key is recognizing the undefended rook on e1 and the passed e-pawn that can advance with check after removing the f2 blocker. Once you capture the f2 pawn with check, you force the king to move, and then promote with check\u2014a devastating move that wins material immediately. When you see a weak pawn in front of the opponent's king, look for ways to remove it and create immediate threats like promotion or checks.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"exf2+\", \"line\": [\"exf2+\", \"Kg2\", \"f1=Q+\", \"Kh2\", \"Qxd3\", \"Rf1\"], \"motifs\": [\"promotion\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRprBP/5P2/4R1K1 b - - 0 31"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRprBP/5P2/4R1K1 b - - 0 31"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRprBP/5P2/4R1K1 b - - 0 31"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRprBP/5P2/4R1K1 b - - 0 31", "move": "exf2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRprBP/5P2/4R1K1 b - - 0 31", "move": "Rxg3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRp1rP/5P2/4R1K1 w - - 0 32", "move": "fxg3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRp1PP/8/4R1K1 b - - 0 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRp1rP/5P2/4R1K1 w - - 0 32", "move": "Kh2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r1k1/1p4pp/8/8/1Pn5/2NRp1rP/5P1K/4R3 b - - 1 32", "move": "Rxh3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_m